      "description": "Watch Brighton vs Aston Villa highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The Premier League International Cup delivered a captivating encounter on August 23, 2026 , as Brighton hosted Aston Villa in a match defined by tactical shifts and high-intensity football. Fans at the stadium witnessed a game where early momentum collided with unexpected disciplinary drama. Early Dominance and Clinical Finishing From the opening whistle, Brighton looked every bit the dominant force. The deadlock was broken in dramatic fashion in the 8th minute when Maxim De Cuyper saw his effort strike the post, only for the rebound to be turned into the net by Victor Lindelof for an own goal. This early breakthrough set the tone for a one-sided first half. By the 18th minute, the lead was doubled; a fluid move involving Lewis Dunk and Georginio Rutter allowed Maxim De Cuyper to slot home a comfortable left-footed finish. The Seagulls continued to press their advantage, effectively ending the contest as a spectacle by the 31st minute. Jack Hinshelwood rose highest to meet a delivery from Diego Gomez , heading home from close range to make it 3-0. Aston Villa struggled to cope with the pace of the game, with defensive lapses from Pau Torres and Ross Barkley frequently inviting pressure from the relentless Brighton attack. Resilience Amid Disciplinary Drama However, the match took an unexpected turn in the 40th minute when Joao Gomes was shown a direct red card following a serious foul. Despite being reduced to ten men, Brighton did not retreat. Instead, they displayed remarkable composure and tactical discipline. Aston Villa introduced Alejandro Garnacho and Matteo Ruggeri in an attempt to spark a comeback, but they found themselves frustrated by a resolute defensive line and a lack of clinical edge in the final third. The second half was punctuated by VAR reviews and tactical substitutions as both managers looked to influence the closing stages. Brighton thought they had added a fourth through Charalampos Kostoulas , but the goal was ruled out for offside. Even with a numerical disadvantage, the hosts controlled 73% of the possession, leaving the visitors chasing shadows. The match concluded with a deserved victory for Brighton , who managed the game expertly until the final whistle."
